From 65f0d06603516c50a0295c582d757f433db49439 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yashgix <125082291+yashgix@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:20:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(wire): ignore topic frames from an attachment the client
 already left

update, topic-gap and topic-error frames carry only the topic, so a frame still in
flight for a closed attachment was applied to a newer attachment of the same topic.
The server now stamps the attach id on these frames and returns it in the attach
result. The client remembers, per topic, the ids it left (its own and the shared
attachment's) and drops frames stamped with one of them. Frames from a shared
attachment, and frames without an id, behave as before.
